/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-62-  // ==== heap allocation (constructed lists become objects) ==================
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-63-  // Cons-form emission with a freshness guard (the heap-list-probe discipline:
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-64-  // an update-form H[N <- _] never re-normalizes symbolically). heapLoc is
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-65-  // monotonic — it does NOT wind back at #pop: returned lists escape by ref.
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k:66:  // A bare list(VS) Val stays legal (read-only inputs in claims flow unboxed);
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-67-  // only CONSTRUCTORS in program syntax allocate.
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-68-  syntax Bool ::= isRefV(Val) [function, total]
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-69-  rule isRefV(ref(_:Int)) => true
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-70-  rule isRefV(_:Val)      => false [owise]
